2020-07-02 Alexander Necheff <alex@necheff.net>
    * Set version to 0.2.2-dev.
    * Changed dynupd to use -z instead of -f as the short option for specifying a zonefile to manage. Fixed issue #32.
    * Corrected an issue with the use of output from the host command in the integration test script. Fixed issue #49.
    * Corrected an issue with dynupd where the last A record would end with EOF instead of a new-line. Fixed issue #48.
    * Corrected an issue with the integration test Docker image preventing zone reloads on successful dynupd requests. Fixed issue #47 and #45.
    * Corrected an issue this dynupd where successful update requests would corrupt the zonefile. Fixed issue #44.
    * Completed base implementation of dynupd; dynupd is now able to ask NSD to reload zones on successful update requests. Fixed issue #25.

2020-07-01 Alexander Necheff <alex@necheff.net>
    * Set version to 0.2.1-dev.
    * Partially automated integration testing by providing a Dockerfile and run scripts. Fixed issue #3.
    * Provided an --addr and --uri option on dynupd to allow the override of default listen address/port and/or URI. Fixed issue #13.
    * Fixed unreported bugs in dynupd which had resulted in an invalid return JSON message.
    * Started developing with 1.14.4 toolchain.

2020-03-21 Alexander Necheff <alex@necheff.net>
    * Set version to 0.2.0-dev.
    * Refactored and overhauled authenticaion system to use erasable byte slices for passwords. Fixed issue #7, #17, and #24.
    * Modified dynupd to partially manually parse the password field of a request using json.RawMessage. Fixed issue #19.
    * Added option to dynupd to override default nsddynpasswd file location. Fixed issue #20.
    * Confirmed that json.Unmarshal returns an error when malformed requests are received. Fixed issue #21.
    * Replaced generic error messages in dynupd with return status codes. Fixed issue #22.
    * Changed nsddynum to treat nsddynpasswd file non-existance as an error, added installation instructions.
        covering the creation of the nsddynpasswd on new installs. Fixed issue #28.
    * Changed nsddynum to use the s/crypto/ssh/terminal package for reading passwords. Fixed issue #29.
    * Fixed a bug where the nsddynum adduser sub-command did not add authorized hosts to the nsddynpasswd file. Fixed issue #30.

2020-02-29 Alexander Necheff <alex@necheff.net>
    * Set version to 0.1.2-dev.
    * Changed API handler internals to support instance state instead of using global variables.
    * Added capability to update zonefile, without authentication.

